#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:2
msgid "How to configure pull request builds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:4
msgid ""
"In this section, you can learn how to configure :doc:`pull request builds </"
"pull-requests>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:6
msgid ""
"Pull request builds are enabled by default on new projects. Your Read the "
"Docs project needs to be connected to a repository from a supported Git "
"provider. See `Limitations`_ for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:10
msgid "To enable or disable pull request builds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:12 ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:61
msgid "Go to your project dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:13 ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:62
msgid "Go to :guilabel:`Settings`, then :guilabel:`Pull request builds`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:14
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the :guilabel:`Build pull requests for this project` option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:15 ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:64
msgid "Click on :guilabel:`Update`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:19
msgid ""
"Pull requests opened before enabling pull request builds will not trigger "
"new builds automatically. Push a new commit to the pull request to trigger "
"its first build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:24
msgid ""
"The previous method of pull request previews using a GitHub workflow that "
"called `@readthedocs/actions <https://github.com/readthedocs/actions/>`__ is "
"now deprecated. If you used that method, you should remove its configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:28
msgid "Build overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:30
msgid ""
"You can enable a build overview comment to be added to your pull requests "
"when changes are detected between the pull request and the latest version of "
"the documentation. This comment includes a list of the files that changed, "
"and links to view the built documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:34
msgid ":ref:`visual-diff:Show build overview in pull requests`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:35
msgid "How to configure your project to enable build overviews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:38
msgid "Privacy levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:42
msgid "Privacy levels are only supported on :doc:`/commercial/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:44
msgid ""
"If you didn’t import your project manually and your repository is public, "
"the privacy level of pull request previews will be set to *Public*, "
"otherwise it will be set to *Private*. Public pull request previews are "
"available to anyone with the link to the preview, while private previews are "
"only available to users with access to the Read the Docs project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:52
msgid ""
"If you set the privacy level of pull request previews to *Private*, make "
"sure that only trusted users can open pull requests in your repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:55
msgid ""
"Setting pull request previews to private on a public repository can allow a "
"malicious user to access read-only APIs using the user's session that is "
"reading the pull request preview. Similar to `GHSA-pw32-ffxw-68rh <https://"
"github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/security/advisories/GHSA-pw32-"
"ffxw-68rh>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:59
msgid "To change the privacy level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:63
msgid ""
"Select your option in :guilabel:`Privacy level of builds from pull requests`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:66
msgid ""
"Privacy levels work the same way as :ref:`normal versions <versions:Version "
"states>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:69
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:71
msgid ""
"Pull requests are only available for **GitHub** and **GitLab** currently. "
"Bitbucket is not yet supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:72
msgid ""
"To enable this feature, your Read the Docs project needs to be connected to "
"a repository from a supported Git provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:73
msgid ""
"If your project is using our :ref:`reference/git-integration:GitHub App`, "
"you don't need to configure a webhook. For GitLab, and projects using our "
"old GitHub integration, you need to make sure that your webhook is "
"configured to send pull request events, not just push events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:75
msgid ""
"Builds from pull requests have the same memory and time limitations :doc:`as "
"regular builds </builds>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:77
msgid "Additional formats like PDF aren't built in order to reduce build time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:78
msgid ""
"Read the Docs doesn't index search on pull request builds. This means that "
"Addons search and the Read the Docs Search API will return no results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:79
msgid ""
"The built documentation is kept for 90 days after the pull request has been "
"closed or merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:80
msgid ""
"The build overview comment is only available for projects connected to a :"
"ref:`reference/git-integration:GitHub App`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:83
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:85
msgid "No new builds are started when I open a pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:86
msgid ""
"The most common cause when using GitHub is that your Read the Docs project "
"is not :ref:`connected to the corresponding repository on GitHub <reference/"
"git-integration:Connect a repository to an existing project>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:89
msgid ""
"If you are using our old GitHub integration, make sure that your "
"repository's webhook is configured to send pull request events. You can re-"
"sync your project's webhook integration to reconfigure the Read the Docs "
"webhook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:94
msgid ""
"To re-sync your project's webhook, go to your project's admin dashboard, :"
"guilabel:`Integrations`, and then select the webhook integration for your "
"provider. Follow the directions to re-sync the webhook, or create a new "
"webhook integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:99
msgid ""
"You may also notice this behavior if your Read the Docs account is not "
"connected to your Git provider account, or if it needs to be reconnected. "
"You can (re)connect your account by going to your :guilabel:`<Username "
"dropdown>`, :guilabel:`Settings`, then to :guilabel:`Connected Services`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:104
msgid "Build status is not being reported to your Git provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:105
msgid ""
"If opening a pull request does start a new build, but the build status is "
"not being updated with your Git provider, then your connected account may "
"have out dated or insufficient permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:109
msgid ""
"Make sure that you have granted access to the Read the Docs `GitHub OAuth "
"App`_ for your personal or organization GitHub account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:113
msgid ":ref:`guides/setup/git-repo-manual:Debugging webhooks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/pull-requests.rst:114
msgid ":ref:`github-permission-troubleshooting`"
msgstr ""
